{
 "id": "MURDER-02",
 "title": "The Dead Man With 'Tamam Shud' in a Hidden Pocket",
 "category": "murder",
 "voice": "am_adam",
 "speed": 1.06,
 "mood": "murder",
 "target_seconds": 72,
 "lines": [
  {
   "id": "L01",
   "text": "This scrap was hidden in a tiny pocket inside a dead man's trousers.",
   "pause_after": 0.25,
   "shot": "S01",
   "emphasis": [
    "hidden",
    "dead"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L02",
   "text": "Two words. Tamam Shud. Persian for, ended.",
   "pause_after": 0.4,
   "shot": "S02",
   "emphasis": [
    "ended"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L03",
   "text": "Somerton Beach, Adelaide. The first of December, 1948.",
   "pause_after": 0.2,
   "shot": "S03",
   "emphasis": [
    "1948"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L04",
   "text": "A well-dressed man, dead against the seawall. No ID.",
   "pause_after": 0.2,
   "shot": "S04",
   "emphasis": [
    "No",
    "ID"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L05",
   "text": "The labels on his clothes had been cut out.",
   "pause_after": 0.3,
   "shot": "S05",
   "emphasis": [
    "labels"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L06",
   "text": "Weeks later, a suitcase linked to him turned up at Adelaide railway station.",
   "pause_after": 0.15,
   "shot": "S06",
   "emphasis": [
    "suitcase"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L07",
   "text": "Its label? Removed too.",
   "pause_after": 0.3,
   "shot": "S07",
   "emphasis": [
    "Removed"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L08",
   "text": "Then someone handed police the very book that scrap was torn from.",
   "pause_after": 0.15,
   "shot": "S08",
   "emphasis": [
    "book"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L09",
   "text": "The Rubaiyat of Omar Khayyam.",
   "pause_after": 0.2,
   "shot": "S09",
   "emphasis": [
    "Rubaiyat"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L10",
   "text": "On the back cover, in pencil: a phone number, and lines of letters.",
   "pause_after": 0.2,
   "shot": "S10",
   "emphasis": [
    "letters"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L11",
   "text": "A code. Nobody has ever cracked it.",
   "pause_after": 0.35,
   "shot": "S11",
   "emphasis": [
    "code",
    "cracked"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L12",
   "text": "Cause of death? Never determined. Poison was suspected. None was found.",
   "pause_after": 0.25,
   "shot": "S12",
   "emphasis": [
    "Poison",
    "None"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L13",
   "text": "Spy. Lost love. Suicide. Plenty of theories, no proof.",
   "pause_after": 0.45,
   "shot": "S13",
   "emphasis": [
    "theories",
    "proof"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L14",
   "text": "Then, in 2021, police exhumed his body.",
   "pause_after": 0.2,
   "shot": "S14",
   "emphasis": [
    "exhumed"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L15",
   "text": "In 2022, a professor and a genealogist tested hairs from his plaster death mask.",
   "pause_after": 0.2,
   "shot": "S15",
   "emphasis": [
    "hairs"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L16",
   "text": "The DNA led through family trees to a name.",
   "pause_after": 0.35,
   "shot": "S16",
   "emphasis": [
    "name"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L17",
   "text": "Carl, Charles, Webb. An electrical engineer from Melbourne, born 1905.",
   "pause_after": 0.45,
   "shot": "S17",
   "emphasis": [
    "Webb"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L18",
   "text": "But it isn't official. Police and the coroner haven't confirmed it yet.",
   "pause_after": 0.3,
   "shot": "S18",
   "emphasis": [
    "official"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L19",
   "text": "And even if he is Webb, no one knows how he died.",
   "pause_after": 0.15,
   "shot": "S19",
   "emphasis": [
    "how"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L20",
   "text": "Or what the code says.",
   "pause_after": 0.35,
   "shot": "S20",
   "emphasis": [
    "code"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L21",
   "text": "So what do you think those letters spell?",
   "pause_after": 0.45,
   "shot": "S21",
   "emphasis": [
    "you"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L22",
   "text": "It all comes back to this.",
   "pause_after": 0.0,
   "shot": "S22",
   "emphasis": [
    "this"
   ]
  }
 ],
